# CH05 — Paper Ghosts. Bellharbor, Sak, the confiscated ledger. SC05 is authored.

@scene T04_POT_CHILD
if event:T04_PIP_OFFER,!flag:t04_distracted alarm
say child | They took our bell. So when the tide's coming in wrong, I bang this pot. Everyone knows the pot now.
end
label alarm
call T04_POT_ALARM
@end

@scene T04_SAILOR
if ch:CH06 run
say sailor | Coastal ferry's tied up. Ministry won't let us sail till the archive business is settled.
end
label run
say sailor | Ferry runs north to Skyspine now. Board at the east pier on the world road.
@end

@scene T04_DOCKHAND
say worker | Seven barrels of lamp oil came in yesterday. Lamp oil doesn't cough.
@end

@scene T04_REFUGEE
say survivor | I came in on a cargo tag. Now I'm here and I don't exist. I'd like to exist again, if it's allowed.
@end

@scene T04_CUSTOMS_GUARD
say guard | Customs house is closed to the public. The public is very annoying today.
@end

@scene T04_FISHWIFE
say baker | Fish, rope, lamp oil. The good charts are down the lane at Jori's.
shop SHOP_T04
@end

@scene T04_CHARTMAKER
say scholar | Charts of every coast from here to the cliffs. Most of them still true, after this summer.
@end

@scene T04_LANE_KID
say child | Jori writes our names down properly. Sak writes them down wrong on purpose. Mum says both are a kind of kindness.
@end

@scene T04_LAMPLIGHTER
say worker | Heartglass lamps on the quay, oil lamps in the lane. The oil ones don't hum.
@end

@scene T04_CHAPLAIN
say monk | Every bell in this chapel is a different size. Every family brought one. None of them match, which is the point.
@end

@scene T04_CHAPEL_REST
say elder | The chapel keeps cots for travellers. We ask a little, if you have it.
inn
@end

@scene T04_JORI
if ch:CH05 after
say jori | Jori. Clerk in practice, if not on paper. I write down who people are. My brother writes down who they aren't.
end
label after
say jori | The families are choosing their own names in the archive record. That's how it should have been from the start.
@end

@scene T04_PIP_OFFER once
say pip | You look like people who need a boat and can't be seen asking for one.
say dain | Who are you?
say pip | Sak. Forger, some say. Logistics, I say. Passage out of Bellharbor, anywhere the tide goes.
say pip | Price: the customs house confiscated a ledger of mine. Get it back and you sail free.
say oriel | What is in the ledger?
say pip | Names. Numbers. The usual paperwork of making people disappear, in a nice way.
say nera | 'In a nice way.'
say pip | There's a nice way! I'll show you. Ledger first.
say pip | The clerk won't leave the counter unless something louder than her happens. Ask the kid with the pot.
objective pip | Recover Sak's confiscated ledger from the customs house (south-west of the quay).
@end

@scene T04_CUSTOMS_CLERK
if flag:t04_distracted gone
say clerk | Customs. Closed. Unless you're filing a complaint, in which case also closed.
if event:T04_PIP_OFFER plan
end
label plan
say narr | The clerk won't leave the counter. Something louder than her would have to happen outside.
end
label gone
say narr | The counter is empty.
@end

@scene T04_POT_ALARM once
say pip | Kid. How'd you like to be a hero of the harbour for exactly one minute?
say child | Is it the pot?
say pip | It's the pot.
sfx FX016
shake 0.3
say narr | CLANG. CLANG. CLANG. Half the quay runs to the water's edge to see what the tide is doing.
set t04_distracted
say pip | Customs clerk will be out looking at the sea. Now or never. Well - now or in a few minutes.
@end

@scene T04_CUSTOMS_GUARD2
say guard | Nobody past the counter.
if flag:t04_distracted fine
end
label fine
say guard | ...the tide's doing WHAT? {m:Shit. |}Stay here. Don't touch anything.
@end

@scene T04_TAKE_LEDGER once
say narr | Behind the counter: the confiscation shelf. A thick ledger, chain unlocked.
key K_CONFISCATED
set t04_ledger
say guard | Hey! That's {m:fucking |}evidence!
say pip | Run. Back alleys. Follow me and don't be where the guards are standing.
warp T04_CHASE start right
say narr | (Being caught only sends you back to the alley mouth. The guards never leave their posts.)
@end

@scene T04_CAUGHT
say guard | Got you -
say pip | Not today. Back the way we came!
warp T04_CHASE start right
@end

@scene CH05_CHASE_END once
say pip | Lost them. Chartmaker lane. My brother's office. Don't tell him I ran.
objective pip | Bring the ledger to Jori's office in Chartmaker Lane.
@end

@scene CH05_SC05 once
say narr | Jori is waiting outside his office. He takes the ledger and opens it without asking.
say pip | Seven barrels of lamp oil. Extremely talkative lamp oil.
say jori | Her name is Senn.
say pip | Not at the checkpoint it is not.
say jori | And when she asks for her wages?
say pip | We work something out.
say jori | You work something out. She waits.
say tessa | Keep the names with the cargo numbers.
say pip | I did.
say jori | Then give them back.
say narr | A woman steps out of the lane. She has been listening.
say "Senn" | Which name am I allowed to use?
say pip | ...Whichever you want. That's - that should be yours.
say "Senn" | Then write it down somewhere the ministry can't cross it out.
say pip | There's an archive under the tide. The drowned archive. Old contracts, older than the ministry. A record there isn't theirs.
say pip | I'll take you. I owe - I owe the paperwork.
join C08
say narr | Sak's Tricks include Pilfer: steal from enemies. The Journal keeps rumors you hear, separate from your objective.
chapter CH05
objective pip | Reach the Drowned Archive, south-east along the coast from Bellharbor, at low water.
discover L_D05
rumor | Sak says the Drowned Archive opens its tide door at low water, south-east of Bellharbor.
level_floor 12
@end
